# {{author_title}} voice

This skill holds {{author_possessive}} measured writing style. It was built on {{built}} from {{n_sources}} of
their own samples ({{n_words}} words). The editing workflow is the `revise-in-voice` skill of the
voice-skill-builder plugin, so it improves whenever the plugin updates and this skill never needs to be
reinstalled for that.

## How to use it

1. `VOICE_DIR` is this skill's folder. Claude Code replaces `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}` in this file with that
   folder when the skill loads; Codex and claude.ai do not, so there use the folder this SKILL.md was
   loaded from.
2. Load the `revise-in-voice` skill (it may be listed as `voice-skill-builder:revise-in-voice`) and follow
   it for the user's request, with `VOICE_DIR` set to `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}`.
3. If no `revise-in-voice` skill is available, do not revise the draft without it. Tell the user that this
   voice skill needs the voice-skill-builder plugin: in claude.ai, Customize > Plugins > Add > Add
   marketplace with `JihuLee/editor-not-ghostwriter`, then add Voice Skill Builder; in Claude Code or
   Codex, `npx skills add JihuLee/editor-not-ghostwriter -g`.

## Files

- `references/author_profile.json`: the measured baseline, recurring slips and settings.
- `references/author_voice.md`: habits, connectives, recurring slips, notes from reading the samples and
  standing requests.
- `references/author_stats.md`: the numbers behind the profile.

To add a standing request or new samples, use the build-voice-skill builder; it rebuilds this skill from
its own files.
